course: french
lesson: 28
title: Être: to be
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Être means "to be", and it is one of the busiest words in French: je suis (I am), tu es (you are), il est and elle est (he is, she is), nous sommes (we are), vous êtes (you are), ils sont and elles sont (they are).
explain: It does not follow any pattern, so French children and English children both learn it by heart, chanting it like a football song on the bus.
explain: Watch the sneaky pair tu es and il est: they sound exactly the same, "ay", but tu takes es and il or elle takes est with a t.
explain: Picture running for the school bus with a French friend who shouts "On est en retard !" - we're late! In talk, French people often use on for "we", with the same verb as il: on est.
explain: Some things English says with "to be" use avoir in French: you have hunger, thirst and years, so "I am hungry" is j'ai faim and "I am nine" is j'ai neuf ans.
fact: Être (to be): je suis, tu es, il est, elle est, on est, nous sommes, vous êtes, ils sont, elles sont; it must be learned by heart.
fact: Je suis une fille and je suis un garçon: être is followed by un or une matching the noun.
fact: Nationalities after être take a small letter and add e for a girl: je suis écossais, je suis écossaise; anglais, anglaise; gallois, galloise.
fact: Tu es and il est sound the same ("ay") but are spelled differently: es with tu, est with il or elle.
fact: After nous sommes, vous êtes, ils sont and elles sont, the describing word is plural: nous sommes contents; if all are girls, contentes.
fact: Ils sont means "they are"; the s of ils is silent before a consonant, so ils sont sounds like "eel SON".
fact: In talk, on often means "we", and it takes the same verb as il: on est, on a, on joue.
fact: Êtes has a little hat, the circonflexe, which remembers an old s; vous êtes sounds "voo-ZET".
fact: C'est is ce plus est squashed together and means "it is" or "that is": C'est super ! C'est mon frère.
fact: Hunger, thirst, fear, heat and cold use avoir, not être: j'ai faim, j'ai soif, j'ai peur, j'ai chaud, j'ai froid.
fact: Age uses avoir: j'ai neuf ans; "je suis neuf" would mean "I am new".
exercise: Which is the right order of être? | je suis, tu es, il est | je es, tu suis, il est | je suis, tu est, il es | je sommes, tu es, il sont
exercise: Ava writes "Je suis un fille." What is right? | Je suis une fille | Je suis un fille | Je suis la fille une | Je es une fille
exercise: Isla, a Scottish girl, writes "Je suis Écossais." What is right? | Je suis écossaise | Je suis Écossaise | Je suis écossais | Je suis Écossaisse
exercise: Harry writes "Il es grand." What is right? | Il est grand | Il es grand | Il et grand | Il sont grand
exercise: Which two sound the same? | tu es and il est | je suis and tu es | nous sommes and ils sont | vous êtes and il est
exercise: Mia says that she and her brother are happy. Which is right? | Nous sommes contents | Nous sommes content | Nous est contents | Nous êtes contents
exercise: Josh writes "Ils est dans le jardin." What is right? | Ils sont dans le jardin | Ils es dans le jardin | Ils suis dans le jardin | Il sont dans les jardin
exercise: Olivia's friend shouts "On est en retard !" What does on mean here? | We | On top | A person called On | Them
exercise: Which verb goes with on? | The same as il: on est | The same as nous: on sommes | The same as je: on suis | The same as ils: on sont
exercise: How do you write "you are" for a group? | vous êtes | vous etes | vous êtez | vous sommes
exercise: What is c'est made of? | ce + est | ces + t | se + est | c + et
exercise: Ella says "Je suis faim." What is right? | J'ai faim | Je suis faimme | Je faim | Je suis la faim
exercise: Leo is nine. Which is right? | J'ai neuf ans | Je suis neuf ans | Je suis neuf | J'ai neuf
exercise: What would "Je suis neuf" mean? | I am new | I am nine | I am hungry | I am tired
exercise: Which says "I am cold"? | J'ai froid | Je suis froid | Je froid | J'ai froide
test: Jacob's mate in Liverpool goes, "Je suis, tu es, il est - sounds like a footy chant, la." Which line keeps the chant going right? | nous sommes, vous êtes, ils sont | nous sont, vous êtes, ils sommes | nous sommes, vous es, ils sont | nous êtes, vous sommes, ils sont
test: Your cousin writes "Tu est mon ami." She goes, "It sounds the same, so who cares, innit?" What's the fix? | Tu es, with no t | Tu et, with no s | Tu ai, like j'ai | Nothing, est is fine with tu
test: Gran in Bristol goes, "That wee hat's everywhere, my lover - why's it on êtes?" What's a true answer? | It remembers an old s that was dropped | It shows the word is said very loudly | It means the word is a question | It's just there to look pretty
test: A cartoon girl from Cardiff says "Je suis Galloise." Her teacher marks one thing. What? | The capital G: it's galloise | The e: it should be gallois | The word suis: it should be ai | Nothing, it's all correct
test: What would happen if you told a French waiter "Je suis faim"? | He'd understand, but French says j'ai faim | He'd think you said your name was Faim | He'd bring you the bill straight away | He'd think you were very full
test: Leo from Brisbane asks, "So is it je suis neuf ans, mate?" What do you tell him? | Age uses avoir: j'ai neuf ans | Yes, je suis neuf ans is right | It's je suis neuf, no ans | It's je es neuf ans
test: Your mate writes "Sest super" about a film. Fix it. | C'est super | S'est super | Cest super | Ces super
test: ★★★ Lucy's two sisters are both happy. Which sentence about them is right? | Elles sont contentes | Ils sont contents | Elles sont contents | Elles est contentes
test: Your US penpal goes, "Ugh, on est? Like, 'on' the table? That's so mid." (mid = not great) What does on mean? | We, in everyday talk | On top of something | Only one person | You, in a polite way
test: ★★★ How many of these are right? je suis, tu est, il est, nous sommes, vous êtes, ils sont | Five | Four | Six | Three
test: Max from Newcastle says, "Howay, c'est is a mash-up!" Of what? | ce (it) and est (is) | c (see) and est (east) | ces (these) and t | se (self) and est (is)
exam: Identify the form of the verb être which corresponds to the pronoun "nous". | sommes | sont | êtes | suis
exam: Select the sentence which correctly expresses, in respect of a female Scottish speaker, her nationality. | Je suis écossaise | Je suis Écossaise | Je suis écossais | J'ai écossaise
exam: Determine the verb employed in French for the expression of hunger. | avoir, as in j'ai faim | être, as in je suis faim | faire, as in je fais faim | aller, as in je vais faim
exam: Ascertain the meaning of the statement "Je suis neuf". | I am new | I am nine years of age | I am hungry | I possess nine items
